<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lazarica Church</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lazarica</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lazarica Church is a medieval Serbian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> church in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krusevac">Kruševac</a>, built in the 1370s or 1380s as the court church of Prince Lazar. Dedicated to Saint Stephen, it is one of the finest examples of the Morava school of architecture, with a trefoil plan and richly carved stone decoration on its façades. It stands in the remains of Lazar's fortress.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lazarica-church.jpg" alt="Lazarica Church" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sun82 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lazarica_Church.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
